Feature: Transition metatype — fields are enums (EventEnum/BranchEnum) and the
emitted taps namespace carries eventToString/branchToString, but no flow-level
spelling can invoke them (KORU104 blocks calls in argument position; a bare
`t.source` arg emits EventEnum into a []const u8 param, which fails zig build).

Missing mechanism: a way to apply the emitted stringifiers — either the
emitter auto-coerces metatype-enum args into string params, or a tor-visible
path to the taps helpers.

Re-spelled 2026-10-13: `~[comptime|runtime]* -> *` -> `~tap(* -> *)`; fails
KORU104 at the real wall instead of KORU010 on dead grammar.
